WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.358 --> 00:00:05.358
(whimsical Latin jazz with whistling)

00:00:05.541 --> 00:00:07.960
(popping)

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:09.170
- Back again! (laughing)

00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:11.440
So last time I tried tiny cooking,

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:14.500
and I feel like I was pretty good at it!

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:17.030
- Looks like I'm gonna tiny bake a cake?

00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:18.180
Bake a tiny cake.

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:20.180
Tiny bake a tiny cake.

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:24.562
- I love baking, but I've
never done a tiny one, so.

00:00:24.562 --> 00:00:25.395
(light jazz music)

00:00:25.395 --> 00:00:27.000
- There's no instructions at all,

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.520
I'm just supposed to make a cake?

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:30.353
Oh, boy.

00:00:30.353 --> 00:00:34.011
First thing, let's grease the pan!

00:00:34.011 --> 00:00:35.850
And I'm just gonna use my fingers,

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:38.550
because I don't see a nice brush.

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:41.140
So I'm just gonna grease the pan.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:43.880
- I'm gonna pour the cake
mix in here. (tapping)

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:46.100
Who knows much cake mix that is?

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:49.840
- I'm gonna say it's two-thirds
stuff to one-third water.

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:51.548
We're gonna start with that.

00:00:51.548 --> 00:00:56.140
- Next thing, next water.

00:00:57.290 --> 00:01:00.030
- Uh, just a little.

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:02.940
Okay, that is way too
much, I already know.

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:05.957
This is gonna be an eggy cake. (laughing)

00:01:05.957 --> 00:01:10.010
- I think it should be, like,
folding like making a ribbons?

00:01:10.010 --> 00:01:13.920
- Okay, I'm gonna pour this
into my greased cake pan.

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:16.080
- We're gonna put the cake in.

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:18.290
We're gonna cover the cake.

00:01:18.290 --> 00:01:20.700
We're gonna light the briquets.

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:22.030
(playful music)

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:23.716
- So I'm gonna, oh, geez.

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:25.016
That's smokin'.

00:01:25.016 --> 00:01:27.050
- (laughing) Smells like
sugar is burning. (laughing)

00:01:27.050 --> 00:01:29.940
- Oh, it's goin', it's definitely rising.

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:33.180
Maybe I overfilled it,
'cause it's like (laughing)

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:35.950
almost at the top of the pan.

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:37.100
- 'Cause this left side you can see

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:38.616
is already gettin' a little burned.

00:01:38.616 --> 00:01:40.550
So I'm gonna try to put it in this corner,

00:01:40.550 --> 00:01:41.890
away from that heat.

00:01:41.890 --> 00:01:43.250
- Oh, no!

00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:45.428
I don't really know how to salvage this.

00:01:45.428 --> 00:01:46.780
(playful, light music)

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:49.600
- So I wanted to make chocolate cake.

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:51.200
And I wanted to make ganache,

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:54.220
so I just brought heavy cream with me.

00:01:54.220 --> 00:01:55.680
- I don't know if I can make a design,

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:57.460
a tiny design with this strawberry.

00:01:57.460 --> 00:01:58.940
I'm tryin' to think.

00:01:58.940 --> 00:02:00.352
- Look at that.

00:02:00.352 --> 00:02:03.000
(popping)

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:04.740
- Yeah, this is what you want.

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:06.150
Ganache should be shiny.

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:09.592
- I should have made the cake taller.

00:02:09.592 --> 00:02:12.925
(thumping and pounding)

00:02:14.102 --> 00:02:17.650
- Okay, oop! (laughing)

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:19.226
Okay, we lost a little!

00:02:19.226 --> 00:02:21.896
- Oh, it's really loose.

00:02:21.896 --> 00:02:24.140
(tinkling piano music)

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:26.924
- Put a little bit of frosting here.

00:02:26.924 --> 00:02:29.140
Sorta act as a cake glue.

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:31.250
- [Alix] Maybe I can try
to fill in this little hole

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:32.549
we have here.

00:02:32.549 --> 00:02:35.012
(wailing)

00:02:35.012 --> 00:02:38.262
(tinkling piano music)

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:43.600
- It actually looks pretty okay.

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:45.150
Not the worst.

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:47.200
- Sprinkles, oh my gosh, so cute.

00:02:48.182 --> 00:02:50.250
My tiny strawberry shortcake.

00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:54.496
- Okay, but my hands always
shakes when I do this.

00:02:54.496 --> 00:02:57.746
(tinkling piano music)

00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:02.390
- It actually tastes
great, tastes like cake!

00:03:02.390 --> 00:03:04.050
- I think the pink saved the cake.

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:07.920
- Mm, you should eat it!

00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:10.390
- Wow.
- Yeah.

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:12.290
- I think I did pretty
good at tiny baking!

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:13.810
- I get the appeal.

00:03:13.810 --> 00:03:15.250
Although, I don't know how people

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:16.920
make these videos on their own.

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:18.322
- Nailed it, again!

00:03:18.322 --> 00:03:22.155
(gently tinkling piano music)

00:03:29.327 --> 00:03:31.652
(logo whooshes)
(hinge squeaks)

